'''almagra''' (al-mā′grä), ''n.'' [< Sp. ''almagra, almagre'' = Pg. ''almagre'', < Ar. ''al-maghrah'', red ocher.] A fine deep-red ocher, with an admixture of purple, used in India for staining the person. {{smaller|It is also sometimes used as a paint, and for polishing silver and glass, under the name of ''Indian red.''}}

